      "content": "I don't understand what you mean by that. I was trying to talk about the logic of existence, not just repeating words. \n\nLook, it’s simpler than that. If we assume that a person's net impact on the world is zero—meaning all the good they do is eventually erased by time or bad things—then there's no mathematical reason to keep playing the game. If existence is a net zero, then ending it is just a neutral move. Don't you see how that's objectively true?",
